{
  "chapter": "context/context-as-budget",
  "tier": "build",
  "notes": [
    "The default allocation policy is 'whoever appends last wins'. This replaces it with a",
    "table that sums and a policy for every row.",
    "Claimants are classified by how they grow. System prompt and tool schemas are constants,",
    "so exceeding them fails the build rather than the request — enforcing a constant at",
    "runtime is an admission that nobody owns it.",
    "The unbounded claimants — history, tool results, retrieved documents, the user's message —",
    "are bounded at the boundary where they enter.",
    "Eviction order is decided in advance: oldest tool results, then oldest history, then",
    "lower-ranked documents, then the user's message. Old facts are cheaper to lose than old",
    "instructions, and the system prompt and tool schemas are never evicted at all.",
    "The output reserve is never lent out, and the leftover window is headroom rather than",
    "capacity waiting to be used. A larger window is permission to send more, not a reason to."
  ],
  "budget": {
    "window": 200000,
    "reserveOutput": 8000,
    "rows": [
      { "claimant": "system", "allocation": 1500, "policy": "fail-build" },
      { "claimant": "schemas", "allocation": 5000, "policy": "fail-build" },
      { "claimant": "documents", "allocation": 12000, "policy": "rerank-and-take-fewer" },
      { "claimant": "results", "allocation": 8000, "policy": "summarize-at-the-tool-boundary" },
      { "claimant": "history", "allocation": 30000, "policy": "compact-oldest-first" },
      { "claimant": "user", "allocation": 2000, "policy": "truncate-with-a-marker" }
    ],
    "evictionOrder": ["results", "history", "documents", "user"]
  },
  "cases": [
